WEBVTT

00:08.500 --> 00:15.700
Omoi wo ima hanadete hatenai asu ni kazasu yo

00:08.500 --> 00:15.700
I now play my feelings,
out to the endless tomorrow!

00:15.740 --> 00:22.450
Setsunai hodo mune utsu kagirinai kibou

00:15.740 --> 00:22.450
This unbounded hope that beats in my breast
to the point of melancholy

00:23.250 --> 00:31.050
Hakanasa wo masu hibi wo
irodoru wa kisetsu no kaze

00:23.250 --> 00:31.050
The days pass by, becoming more fleeting,
colored by the season's wind

00:31.090 --> 00:35.760
Kioku no kakera ga sawagidashita yo

00:31.090 --> 00:35.760
The fragments of memory started running wild

00:36.360 --> 00:44.760
Arinomama wo mitomete
haruka tsumuida hikari ga

00:36.360 --> 00:44.760
One more time, I want to hold the
spindle of far off light close to my breast,

00:44.810 --> 00:52.440
Kieru mae ni mou ichido
kono mune ni dakishimete

00:44.810 --> 00:52.440
Before it disappears, before
I accept the way things are now

00:54.520 --> 01:01.720
Omoi wo ima hanadete hatenai asu ni kazasu yo

00:54.520 --> 01:01.720
I now play my feelings,
out to the endless tomorrow!

01:01.720 --> 01:08.860
Mirai wo egaku ao ni kono te wo nobashite

01:01.720 --> 01:08.860
Hold out this hand to the blue-painted future

01:09.030 --> 01:16.160
Kasokushiteku sekai yo douka
yasashii mama de ite

01:09.030 --> 01:16.160
The world accelerates, please let it stay this kind

01:16.270 --> 01:23.770
Setsunai hodo mune utsu afuredasu negai

01:16.270 --> 01:23.770
This overflowing wish that beats in my breast
to the point of melancholy

01:36.590 --> 01:41.090
Then, you use verb plus the past participle,
and it becomes passive.

01:43.430 --> 01:47.230
Then if you add "by" someone...

01:49.840 --> 01:50.970
Are you all right?

01:50.970 --> 01:53.040
It's just some dogs getting in a fight.

01:53.040 --> 01:55.540
You're such a scaredy-cat, Ichika!

01:55.540 --> 01:57.110
It's nothing to be ashamed of.

01:57.110 --> 02:01.480
This town has a long history, and
it's been the setting for ghost stories.

02:04.790 --> 02:07.220
Along with the beginning of summer

02:07.220 --> 02:11.820
came the mysterious girl from
an old mirror at school, Manatsu.

02:12.590 --> 02:15.090
Could she be a...

02:15.760 --> 02:19.430
Sheesh, Sei. Don't go scaring Ichika all right?

02:19.430 --> 02:21.160
Oh, I apologize.

02:21.970 --> 02:26.470
A rapping noise? The clamoring of spirits?
A poltergeist?

02:26.740 --> 02:28.400
Count me out!

02:36.050 --> 02:37.290
It's a bug.

02:37.290 --> 02:39.190
It must be attracted to the light.

02:50.530 --> 02:55.030
Sudden Shower by the Lake Shore

02:57.270 --> 02:59.110
A summer program?

02:59.110 --> 03:02.840
Yes. It's outside of Ichika's normal schoolwork,

03:02.840 --> 03:06.480
but since you're here, I went
and enrolled you, Manatsu.

03:06.480 --> 03:08.920
Mother, Manatsu is...

03:09.220 --> 03:11.310
What about Manatsu?

03:11.890 --> 03:12.790
Well...

03:13.420 --> 03:16.290
She's not a ghost, right?

03:16.860 --> 03:19.460
But I'm not a student.

03:19.460 --> 03:21.430
Don't worry.

03:21.430 --> 03:23.590
Go and make lots of fond summer memories.

03:26.640 --> 03:29.000
Okay, we're heading off!

03:29.000 --> 03:30.370
Have fun.

03:33.240 --> 03:36.680
Good morning, Ms. Kogure.

03:37.610 --> 03:40.950
Good morning. Where are you going today?

03:41.520 --> 03:44.020
To a summer program for my daughter.

03:44.020 --> 03:45.350
I see.

03:45.350 --> 03:49.020
We'll be at a lake in the mountains
for three days.

03:49.020 --> 03:49.960
Now then...

03:56.230 --> 03:58.390
I can't believe we're doing this.

03:58.700 --> 04:01.840
Is it true this goes on your permanent record?

04:01.840 --> 04:04.470
I've got my cram school work, too...

04:04.470 --> 04:08.180
Non, non! You don't have
the right idea, Tomoko, Yuka!

04:08.180 --> 04:11.150
Summer programs
are supposed to be enjoyable!

04:11.150 --> 04:13.340
Good day to you, Miss Takigawa.

04:17.790 --> 04:19.150
Good day...

04:20.320 --> 04:21.690
What're you so happy about?

04:21.690 --> 04:23.460
Summer programs are for learning,
not playing around!

04:23.460 --> 04:25.760
Summer programs are for learning,
not playing around!
Good Morning.

04:26.060 --> 04:27.650
Good morning.

04:28.000 --> 04:30.230
Good morning Ichika and Manatsu.

04:30.230 --> 04:33.100
You are coming as well, Manatsu?

04:33.100 --> 04:36.730
Yeah... Ichika's mom kind of went and...

04:37.070 --> 04:39.740
That girl is Miss Kuroki, yes?

04:39.740 --> 04:42.380
Yes. Thank you very much.

04:42.380 --> 04:46.140
Well, we had a spot open,
so I'll make a special exception.

04:54.690 --> 04:57.590
I guess the construction has begun...

05:11.870 --> 05:16.370
Let's start walking down a new path!

05:21.780 --> 05:22.980
Thank you!

05:22.980 --> 05:24.790
You're great, Kuroki!

05:24.790 --> 05:26.890
Sing another one, Manatsu!

05:26.890 --> 05:28.690
This time, everyone sing along!

05:28.690 --> 05:29.990
Yeah!

05:31.160 --> 05:33.360
Manatsu is too excited...

05:33.360 --> 05:37.060
Yes. I wonder if it is okay for her
to leave the town?

05:37.870 --> 05:40.100
W-What are you talking about?

05:41.500 --> 05:43.130
Nothing at all.

05:44.440 --> 05:46.440
If Manatsu is a ghost...

05:46.440 --> 05:48.430
A ghost that's tied to a certain place...

05:48.740 --> 05:52.250
Then she shouldn't be able to leave our town.

05:52.250 --> 05:53.610
But...

05:54.550 --> 05:56.450
Sing us a song next, Yuka!

05:56.450 --> 05:58.020
I guess she isn't a ghost.

05:58.020 --> 05:59.250
I guess she isn't a ghost.

05:59.250 --> 06:00.620
Who isn't?

06:00.620 --> 06:02.090


06:02.090 --> 06:04.220
Oh, never mind!

06:26.950 --> 06:28.650
Yes, this is the Toudou residence.

06:28.650 --> 06:32.140
Oh, Mrs. Tachibana? No, it's okay.

06:32.450 --> 06:35.120
I'm sorry I forgot to inform you.

06:35.120 --> 06:37.790
I know you were scheduled to come
and tutor today and tomorrow, but...

06:38.990 --> 06:40.460
Canceling?

06:40.960 --> 06:42.760
Okay, we understand.

06:42.760 --> 06:44.530
Then, if you'll excuse me...

06:44.530 --> 06:45.430
What was it?

06:45.700 --> 06:49.770
Ichika and Manatsu are at a
summer program for three days.

06:49.770 --> 06:50.930
Manatsu?

06:51.570 --> 06:52.630
That girl?

06:53.280 --> 06:54.830
I hope they'll be okay...

06:55.480 --> 06:58.810
Ichika gets scared easily.

07:00.250 --> 07:02.880
Isn't that true for a certain someone, too?

07:04.650 --> 07:08.090
Wow! We're out of cellphone range!

07:08.090 --> 07:11.150
Whoa, no way! We could connect
at the place we were last year.

07:11.630 --> 07:13.320
It's no use.

07:14.160 --> 07:15.130
We're here!

07:16.430 --> 07:18.090
What's the matter, Ichika?

07:18.730 --> 07:22.330
You're not a local ghost then, Manatsu?

07:23.310 --> 07:25.740
Wait, what the heck were you thinking?

07:26.340 --> 07:28.210
I-I'm sorry.

07:28.210 --> 07:29.310
Okay!

07:29.310 --> 07:32.250
Everyone split into groups
and head toward their bungalow.

07:32.250 --> 07:33.920
First, clean it up!

07:33.920 --> 07:35.880
Yes, Ma'am!

07:40.620 --> 07:41.920
Here we are!

07:41.920 --> 07:43.690
1 win!

07:43.690 --> 07:45.160
Wait, Manatsu!

07:46.030 --> 07:46.960
What?

07:46.960 --> 07:48.860
Uh, the floor...

07:51.170 --> 07:53.200
Tell me before hand, sheesh!

07:53.200 --> 07:56.270
There wasn't a chance to.

07:56.270 --> 07:58.600
Well, better get cleaning.

07:59.040 --> 08:01.130
Satsuki, Keiko...

08:01.510 --> 08:03.570
You are in the next group over.

08:08.050 --> 08:09.720
Thanks!

08:09.720 --> 08:11.820
What's with those two?

08:11.820 --> 08:13.980
It seems they got the wrong bungalow.

08:14.290 --> 08:16.390
Finish up the cleaning quickly, okay?

08:16.390 --> 08:18.430
This is where you'll be sleeping, after all.

08:18.430 --> 08:20.430
Okay!

08:20.430 --> 08:22.730
Man, this sucks.

08:22.730 --> 08:26.840
If we were normal guests the staff
would have cleaned it for us.

08:26.840 --> 08:28.830
I guess the place isn't so popular.

08:29.640 --> 08:33.400
You sure are a stickler, Tachibana.

08:35.840 --> 08:39.510
Ichika hates it when people lie or slack off.

08:40.180 --> 08:41.850
Better to take it easy.

08:41.850 --> 08:42.720
You can say that again.

08:44.920 --> 08:47.350
Has this group finished cleaning?

08:47.720 --> 08:49.120
Yes!

08:49.120 --> 08:52.260
What? You're not even close.

08:52.260 --> 08:55.390
I see you're taking this seriously,
Tachibana. I'm impressed.

08:57.570 --> 09:00.030
Anyway, cleaning time is over.

09:00.040 --> 09:01.940
Gather at the meeting place.

09:01.940 --> 09:02.870
But we haven't...

09:02.870 --> 09:04.840
Stop cleaning, even if you're in the middle of it.

09:04.840 --> 09:06.310
It's time to study.

09:06.310 --> 09:07.270
'Kay!

09:07.280 --> 09:08.380
Let's go.

09:08.380 --> 09:09.540
Free at last.

09:11.680 --> 09:13.150
She said we're done.

09:13.150 --> 09:14.270
Let's go, Ichika.

09:21.260 --> 09:23.290
Did everyone bring their materials?

09:23.290 --> 09:26.560
Anyone who forgot theirs,
please take these printouts I prepared.

09:29.000 --> 09:32.030
So it's basically a cram school
for our summer homework.

09:32.030 --> 09:33.830
Feels like detention.

09:33.840 --> 09:35.930
Work hard everyone!

09:36.570 --> 09:37.630
Miss Kuroki.

09:38.440 --> 09:41.430
I don't know about the curriculum
at your school,

09:41.810 --> 09:44.400
but since you've joined us
at this summer program...

09:47.220 --> 09:49.620
Work hard!

09:54.420 --> 09:57.590
Why do I have to do something like this?

09:58.430 --> 10:02.060
I don't have time to be doing
homework for school.

10:02.060 --> 10:04.400
Let's secretly do our cram school work instead.

10:13.210 --> 10:15.580
Go and make lots of fond summer memories.

10:16.740 --> 10:18.840
These memories aren't...

10:23.590 --> 10:25.120
What is it, Ichika?

10:25.120 --> 10:26.090
Um...

10:26.090 --> 10:26.990
Bathroom?

10:27.890 --> 10:30.930
The bathrooms aren't in that direction.

10:30.930 --> 10:33.390
What's Miss Stickler planning?

10:41.670 --> 10:43.240
After that, then...

10:43.240 --> 10:47.040
You sure are a stickler, Tachibana.

10:50.680 --> 10:52.910
A stickler?

11:10.500 --> 11:13.200
Okay, studying time is over!

11:15.200 --> 11:16.170
Here I go!

11:22.580 --> 11:25.550
It's wet over there, be careful!

11:27.580 --> 11:29.850
It's quite muddy.

11:29.850 --> 11:32.650
That's because there hasn't
been much rain recently.

11:32.650 --> 11:34.820
And human pollution, too.

11:41.700 --> 11:44.500
Hey, where'd you girls come from?

11:44.500 --> 11:45.700
This way.

11:45.700 --> 11:48.040
What're your names? I'm Adachi.

11:48.040 --> 11:48.940
I'm Baba.

11:48.940 --> 11:50.130
Wanna chat?

11:51.240 --> 11:52.600
What should we do?

12:18.000 --> 12:19.230
Miss Tachibana.

12:19.530 --> 12:20.470
Yes?

12:20.940 --> 12:22.840
I'd like you to help me with something.

12:23.670 --> 12:25.070
A test of courage?

12:25.370 --> 12:26.540
Yes.

12:26.540 --> 12:28.310
It's pretty standard.

12:29.340 --> 12:33.110
So Michiru and Ichika
are helping to scare people?

12:33.110 --> 12:33.840
Yes.

12:34.280 --> 12:37.320
You're one of those people with "the vision"
after all, Michiru.

12:37.320 --> 12:40.550
I bet tests of courage aren't very fun for you.

12:41.620 --> 12:43.750
That is not the case.

12:45.260 --> 12:46.920
Good luck!

12:48.060 --> 12:50.830
Try and scare us a little, okay?

12:50.830 --> 12:52.160
Yeah...

12:53.370 --> 12:56.540
Okay, we're going to start!

12:56.540 --> 12:57.970
The rules are simple.

12:57.970 --> 13:00.010
Take this card and head down
the path I said, then return here.

13:00.080 --> 13:03.850
What's the point of doing a test of courage
if it's not with a guy?

13:05.250 --> 13:08.550
And it's the time he said to meet up.

13:09.720 --> 13:12.880
Adachi looked like he had
a thing for you, Tomoko.

13:13.350 --> 13:16.290
Okay, I'll cover for you.

13:16.290 --> 13:17.490
Thanks.

13:22.130 --> 13:24.200
Are you ready?

13:24.200 --> 13:27.860
Yes. But it's getting cloudy.

13:28.170 --> 13:32.970
A moonless night may be fine weather
for a test of courage.

13:36.180 --> 13:38.870
I wish I'd brought a flashlight with me.

13:39.710 --> 13:42.950
He's late. I hope I got the right place.

13:47.820 --> 13:49.660
Ow!

13:49.660 --> 13:51.390
How awful!

13:51.390 --> 13:53.550
Who pushed me?

13:54.000 --> 13:55.720
Tomoko, are you here?

13:56.560 --> 13:57.690
Not here yet?

13:58.000 --> 14:01.000
No... I can't let him see me
covered in mud like this.

14:01.000 --> 14:03.170
Maybe she stood me up.

14:03.170 --> 14:04.470
But I came!

14:04.470 --> 14:06.640
Hurry up and leave already...

14:06.640 --> 14:08.610
Oh, Adachi! Picking up some things?

14:08.610 --> 14:10.480
Yeah, something like that.

14:10.480 --> 14:12.310
Same for me. Let's go together.

14:14.880 --> 14:16.110
I guess.

14:23.590 --> 14:25.060
This sucks.

14:33.470 --> 14:36.070
It's just a pitfall filled with urethane...

14:36.070 --> 14:37.970
You're such a scaredy-cat, Keiko!

14:37.970 --> 14:39.340
But...

14:40.940 --> 14:43.040
No!

14:43.040 --> 14:45.110
Stay away!

14:45.110 --> 14:47.580
Save me!

14:49.820 --> 14:52.220
It's our turn next...

14:52.890 --> 14:54.760
Y-yeah...

14:54.760 --> 14:56.560
Oh, where's Tomoko?

14:56.560 --> 14:58.360
The bathroom I guess.

14:58.360 --> 15:01.260
Oh well, it's just the two of us then.

15:01.260 --> 15:02.890
Roger...

15:07.770 --> 15:11.410
What? There's nothing here...

15:11.410 --> 15:13.270
I knew those kiddy little tricks won't...

15:15.410 --> 15:18.070
Kuroki, you're way too on edge.

15:18.650 --> 15:21.250
N-no way!

15:21.250 --> 15:22.050
Oh yeah?

15:22.050 --> 15:25.820
Obviously, yeah! I'm just putting on an act!
Yeah, an act!

15:25.820 --> 15:28.080
In this day and age girls need to be cute and...

15:30.630 --> 15:31.990
I see.

15:33.800 --> 15:35.060
I see.

15:36.430 --> 15:40.060
Cute girls are actually kind of annoying.

15:40.970 --> 15:45.440
Manatsu clearly isn't a ghost if she acts like that.

15:45.440 --> 15:46.440
All that's left is...

15:46.440 --> 15:48.780
Okay, finished!

15:48.780 --> 15:51.080
The test of courage is over!

15:51.080 --> 15:52.100
Huh?

15:56.380 --> 15:57.720
Where's Tomoko?

16:00.020 --> 16:02.720
Promise to keep it a secret from the teacher.

16:03.020 --> 16:03.750
Okay?

16:04.130 --> 16:04.990
Okay...

16:05.290 --> 16:09.260
Tomoko went over to hang out with the
high school students camping next door.

16:09.260 --> 16:11.560
But don't you think it's getting late?

16:11.970 --> 16:13.960
Miss Stickler strikes again...

16:15.270 --> 16:17.140
Is everyone accounted for?

16:17.940 --> 16:20.740
Yes, we're all here!

16:20.740 --> 16:22.000
Don't tell her, sheesh!

16:22.910 --> 16:24.910
Lights out in ten minutes, okay?

16:24.910 --> 16:26.280
'Kay!

16:26.280 --> 16:28.270
Well, they're of that age.

16:32.450 --> 16:33.990
Man, this sucks!

16:33.990 --> 16:35.290
What the hell?

16:43.230 --> 16:45.530
You've got to be kidding me...

16:46.670 --> 16:48.000
I apologize.

16:59.780 --> 17:06.950
I wonder why I couldn't help but feel
a deep unease at that time?

17:08.490 --> 17:10.690
It's started to rain.

17:10.690 --> 17:13.590
Then she must be staying over
at the guy's place.

17:13.590 --> 17:16.690
But you're not going to be able to cover for her
during the morning call.

17:17.000 --> 17:19.700
I'm sure she'll be back before breakfast.

17:26.610 --> 17:30.140
Is there anyone there?

17:30.140 --> 17:31.700
Somebody!

17:34.650 --> 17:37.210
I'm telling you, let it rest.

17:42.690 --> 17:43.520
Ichika!

17:45.030 --> 17:46.080
Are you okay?

17:46.860 --> 17:48.460
I'm okay.

17:48.460 --> 17:49.220
But...

17:52.570 --> 17:54.740
Shouldn't we tell the teacher?

17:54.740 --> 17:59.170
I promised I wouldn't tell the teacher.

17:59.170 --> 18:00.070
Then...

18:36.310 --> 18:37.780
The Water Djinn, Aqua...

18:38.210 --> 18:39.340
The spirit of water...

18:39.650 --> 18:40.980
Please!

18:40.980 --> 18:44.720
Tomoko, my friend, has not come back!

18:44.720 --> 18:46.990
Something might have happened to her!

18:46.990 --> 18:50.420
Please, lend me your power!

19:12.710 --> 19:17.410
Sola, Luna, Terra... The fourth would be Aqua.

19:24.530 --> 19:25.930
What is this?

19:25.930 --> 19:29.860
Rain... You've borrowed
the vision of the raindrops.

19:29.860 --> 19:30.800
The rain?

19:43.410 --> 19:44.510
There she is!

19:44.510 --> 19:45.340
Where?

19:58.730 --> 19:59.850
Tomoko!

20:02.000 --> 20:03.760
Grab onto this!

20:03.760 --> 20:04.700
Okay!

20:08.470 --> 20:10.640
I can't... It's too slippery!

20:10.640 --> 20:11.440
Your hand!

20:11.440 --> 20:13.440
Ichika, that's dangerous!

20:13.440 --> 20:14.100
Manatsu!

20:14.410 --> 20:16.040
Hold me down!

20:16.740 --> 20:17.940
Right.

20:19.680 --> 20:20.980
Tomoko!

20:54.380 --> 20:56.780
Tachibana, are you still awake?

20:59.690 --> 21:02.660
Thanks to you being such a stickler,
I was saved.

21:04.090 --> 21:06.320
But please don't tell the teacher.

21:06.630 --> 21:08.930
Please? Okay?

21:08.930 --> 21:09.900
I won't.

21:09.900 --> 21:10.860
Thank you.

21:15.540 --> 21:21.870
It seems like ever since this summer started
I've been lying more and more.

21:23.680 --> 21:28.240
At that time, my mind was filled only
with thoughts of myself.

21:28.820 --> 21:34.690
I didn't notice Manatsu's crying heart
even a little bit.

21:38.630 --> 21:41.820
I hope Ichika and Manatsu are all right.

21:42.130 --> 21:45.070
Us worrying about them
isn't going to do any good.

21:45.070 --> 21:47.300
We're already...

21:47.570 --> 21:50.590


21:51.210 --> 22:00.770
Ano hi deawanakereba ima mo
waraeteta no ka na?

21:51.210 --> 22:00.770
If we hadn't met that day,
would I have still been able to laugh now?

22:02.150 --> 22:13.650
Ano hi nakushita egao itsuka tokeru namida

22:02.150 --> 22:13.650
The smile I lost that day,
the tears that one day melt away...

22:19.170 --> 22:28.940
Hora kotoshi mo ame furu gogo
hakanai utakata no iro

22:19.170 --> 22:28.940
See, this year the afternoon rain falls again
in the color of fleeting bubbles

22:30.010 --> 22:38.850
Sora mo yasashiku mienai wa
datte hitori da mono

22:30.010 --> 22:38.850
The sky doesn't look kind to me, after all,
I'm alone

22:40.490 --> 22:45.490
Itazura na sadame ni kotoba mo denai wa

22:40.490 --> 22:45.490
I have no more words for the tricks of fate

22:45.890 --> 22:53.290
Wakariaeta futari ni mou modorenai no?

22:45.890 --> 22:53.290
Can we never return to two
who understood each other?

22:53.870 --> 23:03.470
Ano hi deawanakereba ima mo
waraeteta no ka na?

22:53.870 --> 23:03.470
If we hadn't met that day,
would I have still been able to laugh now?

23:04.850 --> 23:16.550
Ano hi nakushita egao itsuka tokeru namida

23:04.850 --> 23:16.550
The smile I lost that day,
the tears that one day melt away...

23:20.590 --> 23:20.690


23:20.690 --> 23:21.460


23:24.960 --> 23:26.060
One's life is led experiencing
a myriad of different feelings.

23:26.630 --> 23:31.130
On that day I came to realize that a
large number of feelings swirl together

23:32.040 --> 23:34.410
in places where a great deal of people gather.

